\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Workflow used to construct the building-level exposure-proxy target. Parcel records provide building-type and unit heuristics; xBD footprints supply building geometry; and CBG boundaries link each building to ACS occupancy and people-per-unit attributes. Their building-level combination produces the Stage\nobreakspace  {}2a training target, which is treated throughout this paper as a constructed exposure proxy rather than an observed count of occupants.}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
