\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Building-level evidence and coverage-aware spatial delivery. (a) A representative Harris County validation record shows the Stage\nobreakspace  {}2a type prediction, constructed exposure proxy, and model estimate in proxy-occupancy units; this panel is from a separate study area from the Los Angeles application. (b) A persistent Los Angeles building is linked across pre- and post-event imagery and retains its coverage-aware multi-date (M2b) damage record. (c) M2b outputs for the surrounding 600-m cell. (d) M2b synthesis for the eastern Los Angeles study area, with not-identifiable buildings retained separately from no visible damage. The flood-trained damage model was applied without wildfire-specific retraining, so panels (b)--(d) demonstrate traceable spatial delivery and coverage handling rather than validated wildfire-damage accuracy.}}{13}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:instance_evidence_outputs}{{5}{13}{Building-level evidence and coverage-aware spatial delivery. (a) A representative Harris County validation record shows the Stage~2a type prediction, constructed exposure proxy, and model estimate in proxy-occupancy units; this panel is from a separate study area from the Los Angeles application. (b) A persistent Los Angeles building is linked across pre- and post-event imagery and retains its coverage-aware multi-date (M2b) damage record. (c) M2b outputs for the surrounding 600-m cell. (d) M2b synthesis for the eastern Los Angeles study area, with not-identifiable buildings retained separately from no visible damage. The flood-trained damage model was applied without wildfire-specific retraining, so panels (b)--(d) demonstrate traceable spatial delivery and coverage handling rather than validated wildfire-damage accuracy}{figure.5}{}}
